# LGR regression baseline: fork (builds/refined) vs upstream master (builds/release).
# Columns: <deck>  <fork==master tol>  <fork-serial==fork-parallel tol>
# Values: 1e-6..1e-1 = tightest matching relative tolerance; Lnz = summaries
#         differ only in length (ministep count) but the field rates agree, i.e.
#         timestep-path noise rather than a solution change; FAIL = field rates
#         genuinely diverge; "-" = a run did not complete.
#
# lgr_regression.sh exits non-zero if any cell here regresses. Lnz ranks just
# above FAIL (it is not a regression). Both flow binaries share opm-simulators,
# so the master binary carries the same simulator-side fixes (e.g. the LGR
# well-cell mapping rebuild) -- this isolates the *grid* difference.
#
# Current state (2026-06-14, after the LGR well-cell-mapping fix):
#   * Cartesian LGR (CARFIN, CARFIN1) and corner-point LGR without faults
#     (2D/3D CORNERPOINT, FLEX): fork == master to 1e-6 on the solution.
#     The earlier corner-point "divergence" was dominated by the well-cell bug
#     (fork-fixed vs master-unfixed); with the fix in both, the small sub-cell
#     geometry difference does not move the solution. The fork is still the
#     geometrically correct one (centre-of-mass conservation, locked by
#     tests/cpgrid/grdecl_refinement_test.cpp::slantedPillarRefinementConservesCenterOfMass).
#   * 3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ ser==par is Lnz: parallel cell numbering nudges the
#     timestep controller onto a different ministep count, but the field rates
#     agree. Stabilising the controller is a separate task; more accurate linear
#     solves (e.g. --linear-solver-reduction=1e-6) make ser and par take the
#     identical Newton path, but not uniformly across decks.
#   * CARFIN_GR: its LGR1 spans the FULL 10x10x3 grid, so the rank-interior
#     model cannot keep the box on one rank without leaving another empty. Serial
#     agrees with master (Lnz); the parallel run now fails *cleanly* with an
#     actionable error (CpGridVanguard guard) instead of the previous SIGABRT.
#     Running such a whole-grid LGR in parallel would need distributed refinement
#     (a box split across ranks), which the fork does not implement; master does.
#     ser==par stays "-" (parallel intentionally does not complete).
#   * 3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ-NON and CARFIN_FAULTS: do not run (the latter fails in
#     opm-common FAULTS parsing, unrelated to the grid; faulted corner-point LGR
#     is suspect in master anyway).
#
#
# 2026-09-05 (host transmissibility on by default, opm-simulators 8d902abbe):
#   * The corner-point decks and AQUFETP now show fork==master FAIL and
#     CARFIN1 ser==par Lnz. Checked by hand: the fork's summaries (with the
#     flag on AND off) are identical to master's on every common report row
#     (FOPR, FPR); only the ministep count differs (e.g. 148 vs 151), and
#     the script's field-rate fallback misaligns rows on these decks, so it
#     reports FAIL where the answer is Lnz. Recorded as the script reports
#     it until the fallback is fixed; do not read these FAILs as a solution
#     change.
#   * 3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ-NON now runs; serial and np=2 field rates differ by
#     2 % with the flag on and 2.5 % off -- pre-existing, not attributed.
#   * AQUNUM_IN_LGR is refused (deck aquifer inside the box) on every rank.
#
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN                          1e-6  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1                         1e-6  Lnz
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-2DCORNERPOINT_XY        FAIL  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ       FAIL  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ-NON   -     FAIL
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_FLEX                     1e-6  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_GR                       Lnz   -
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_FAULTS                   -     -
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1_AQUFETP                 FAIL  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1_AQUNUM                  -     1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1_AQUNUM_IN_LGR           -     -
